{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794869523660699513,"compiled_state":{"alias":"undefeated-famed-platypus","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"a026dfc24402e420073ea9383070d37bff8c8e1401002ccf6552e38be7319d0f","event_uuid":"d2db3797-84da-484c-929f-76d664bcebaa","position":{"commit_sha":"27189dd1557e00ec4085f3e459b542ae8d01072b","position":"1794869109450205794-d2db3797-84da-484c-929f-76d664bcebaa"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"150997b4aad1bb5dd2d12e7a4f601d0c3004b74284deed7e66efe4b9cf4b0f83","event_uuid":"a8ad3369-9bb4-43af-8e47-5a06cf279687","position":{"commit_sha":"390ad6bd863ce15772788fb764ec7731a123a8bc","position":"1794869123932745372-a8ad3369-9bb4-43af-8e47-5a06cf279687"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"906bfa89d5acd41c8003102e2d9261703b40a27212e6484673cd6b8b8e47855a","event_uuid":"47fbd7a0-3079-40a5-93ec-bed7271f7826","position":{"commit_sha":"3a5e7c8def2c4ee2051c99b6e57ac38239145043","position":"1794869523660699512-47fbd7a0-3079-40a5-93ec-bed7271f7826"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Another instance, 2026-11-16 (worktree cb1b-gate-async-starters, b4e0d01b649 + an MCP-only change, load avg 17-44): `make verify` default tier `1 failed, 21306 passed, 29 skipped in 10519.99s`. The only failure was tests/scripts/test_observability_interrupt_reasons.py::test_each_reason_counter_keeps_its_own_offset, with the same `TimeoutExpired` after 60 s from `run_observability`. The file alone at load ~11: `5 passed in 43.71s`. So a third observability test file is affected, not only the two listed above.","timestamp":1794869523660699512}],"created_at":1794869109450205794,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a8ad3369-9bb4-43af-8e47-5a06cf279687","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ab03-0276-374b-46af"}],"description":"## Observation\nA full `make verify` on macOS/arm64 (worktree fix-bd66-detector-flake, origin/main b4e0d01b649 plus a test-only change to tests/unit/test_store_commit_maintenance_bd66.py, `PYTEST_WORKERS=4`, 2026-11-16, host load average 40-70 on 18 CPUs with other sessions' verifies running) ended `4 failed, 21291 passed, 29 skipped in 10796.46s (2:59:56)`:\n\n- tests/scripts/test_observability_reviewbot_webhook_auth.py::test_reviewbot_webhook_auth_rejections_publish_from_health_payload\n- tests/scripts/test_observability_rotation_2dc7.py::test_shrinking_journal_publishes_zero_not_the_remaining_total[replication_errors-REPL_OFFSET_FILE]\n- tests/scripts/test_observability_rotation_2dc7.py::test_shrinking_journal_publishes_zero_not_the_remaining_total[voter_errors-VOTER_OFFSET_FILE]\n- tests/scripts/test_observability_rotation_2dc7.py::test_markers_after_a_rotation_still_publish\n\nAll 4 raised `subprocess.TimeoutExpired: Command '['bash', '.../infra/scripts/observability.sh']' timed out after 60 seconds` from `run_observability(..., timeout=60)`. The same 2 files run alone right after: `10 passed in 89.99s`.\n\n## What is not established\nWhy one stubbed observability.sh run takes over 60 s under load (the stubs replace curl/aws/journalctl). Candidates to distinguish: per-run process count of the script (many short subprocesses, each slowed by load), a stub that blocks, or lock/sleep waits inside the script.\n\n## Approach\nReproduce deterministically (scale the 60 s bound down, or measure the script's subprocess count and wall time per run), identify the cost driver, and fix the class: bound what the test asks the script to do rather than raising the wall-clock bound. No production behaviour change unless the cost is in the script itself.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The cost driver of a stubbed observability.sh run is measured and recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] The 4 tests pass with the cause fixed at class level, without raising the 60 s bound and without retries.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8613-902c-a4cd-4d80","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Flaky: observability.sh tests time out at their 60 s subprocess bound under full-suite load","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d2db3797-84da-484c-929f-76d664bcebaa","a8ad3369-9bb4-43af-8e47-5a06cf279687","47fbd7a0-3079-40a5-93ec-bed7271f7826"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794869523660699513,"uuid":"6b408d10-f375-412a-ad46-37351b1a35e4"}
